      "pronunciationText": "Our question: how does the time of gentle heating affect the percentage of mass lost by the crystals? Now imagine a rushed test. Three people heat some crystals on three different burners, for two, four and six minutes, and weigh them while they're still hot. They lose nineteen, fifteen and thirty-one percent. The four minute sample lost less than the two minute one. Is the hypothesis wrong, or the test? With so many differences at once, we can't tell. The plan decides whether data can answer the question at all.",
