      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "A valid investigation measures what it claims to measure. Here, that means the mass lost must be water, and only the heating time can change it. Heating time is the independent variable, the one we change. The percentage of mass lost is the dependent variable, the one we measure. Everything else that could change the result is a controlled variable, kept the same. The same two point five zero grams of crystals, the same crucible, the same small blue flame at the same height, and the same cooling before each weighing. If any of these changed too, we couldn't tell which change caused the result. And the flame stays gentle, because strong heat would break down the copper sulfate, so the mass lost wouldn't be just water.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
