      "pronunciationText": "Next, reliable data. Reliable means that if you repeat the whole experiment, you get consistent results. So the plan uses three separate samples. Each one is heated in two minute steps, and weighed after every step, from zero to twelve minutes. If all three runs show the same pattern, we can trust it. And seven time points can show where the curve levels off. With only two points, we'd never see it.",
