      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "The nought point zero one gram balance. Count the steps. On the coarse balance, the whole loss is only nine steps, so one step is more than a tenth of the answer. On the finer balance, it's ninety steps, and one step is only about one percent. We choose the other materials the same way. A porcelain crucible, because it survives a direct flame. A lid, set slightly ajar, to stop crystals spitting out while steam still escapes. And tongs, because the crucible gets far too hot to touch.",
