      "pronunciationText": "Planning also means thinking about ethical issues. Copper sulfate is very toxic to life in rivers and the sea, so the white powder goes into a labelled waste container, never down the sink. Using just two point five zero grams per sample keeps the waste small. And every reading goes into the record, including the odd ones. Leaving out results that don't fit would make the data look better than it is.",
