      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "The independent variable is the volume of water. The dependent variable is the percentage of the mixture recovered as salt. Controlled variables include the mass of mixture, the water temperature, the stirring time and the drying. Temperature must stay the same, because warmer water dissolves a little more salt, so it would change the result too. Writing \"the salt\" as a controlled variable is the classic slip. It doesn't say what's kept the same.",
