      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Strong heat breaks down the copper sulfate itself, so the mass lost isn't just water, and the result isn't valid. It can also release irritating gases. So use a small, gentle flame and heat to constant mass. And copper sulfate is toxic to aquatic life, so the powder goes into a waste container, not the sink. Adding \"be careful\" is the classic slip. It doesn't change the likelihood or the harm, so it isn't a control.",
